Revision history for URI-Shorten

2.000 2026-11-24 TEODESIAN
    - The default algorithm for ciphers is now ff1, not fortuna.
      ff1 is the FF1 format-preserving cipher of NIST SP 800-38G, with AES.
      Each row ID gets a different cipher, so new rows do not collide with each other.
      To keep the old ciphers, give algorithm => 'fortuna' to new().
    - Existing databases: stored ciphers do not change, so old short URIs continue to work.
      New rows get ff1 ciphers if you do not set algorithm.
      A new cipher can be the same as an old fortuna cipher in the database.
      Then shorten() burns that row and uses the next row ID.
      Each old cipher can cause this one time at most.
    - The ff1 key comes from HMAC-SHA256 of the seed, so a seed can be any string.
    - For ff1, cipher() dies with "space exhausted" when the row ID is length(domain) ** length or more.
    - For ff1, new() dies when the domain has a character two times,
      or when length(domain) ** length is less than 1,000,000.
      For fortuna, new() dies when the seed is not a number.
    - new() dies when algorithm is not 'ff1' or 'fortuna'.
    - Add decipher(), which gives the row ID of an ff1 cipher.
    - Correct the number of possible URIs in the POD.
      For the defaults it is 52 ** 12, which is 390,877,006,486,250,192,896.
    - Bring the code to the harness standards for perlcritic.
    - The constructor now dies when a table or index name is not a plain SQL identifier.
    - The limit of 64 cipher collisions is now for each call to shorten().
      Before, the count was for the whole process and did not go back to zero.
      A process that ran for a long time died on each collision after the 64th.
    - A burned row now gets a uri that ends in "-BURNED-" and its row ID.
      Before, a second burn of the same URI in a new process used the same uri again.
      Then shorten() died with "Could not burn row" on sqlite and Postgres.
    - The metadata again lists DBD::SQLite as a prerequisite of the tests.
      The build did not read prereqs.yml, so the tests failed where DBD::SQLite was not installed.
    - The tarball no longer contains the git hooks, CLAUDE.md, dist.ini, weaver.ini and prereqs.yml.

